// stdlib/qforge/fixtures/migration_gate_anchors.hexa — QFORGE migration-gate
// 3-anchor cross-validation FIXTURE (CaH6 · LaH10 · Li2MgH16).
//
// ── ROLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The QFORGE→QE migration default-flip (d_qforge_engine) is gated on a 3-anchor
// {λ, Tc} cross-validation matrix: for each high-Tc hydride anchor, QFORGE-NC's
// computed (λ, Tc) must reproduce the terminal QE-DFPT (λ, Tc) to the same g5
// rel-ε bar the L3 YH10 xval uses (≤ 1%). This fixture is the DURABLE machinery:
// it carries the per-anchor QE-reference moments (verbatim from terminal RTSC-
// campaign JSON) plus a `status` flag. `qforge_migration_gate_test.hexa` ingests
// this, computes the QFORGE-NC side live, and emits per-anchor PASS/FAIL +
// aggregate ALL_PASS / HELD.
//
// ── HONESTY (d6/@L4·@L6) — zero fabricated λ·Tc ──────────────────────────────
// Only an anchor whose QE-reference {λ, Tc} is a REAL terminal record is marked
// "terminal". CaH6 is terminal (rtsc_cah6_dft_4x4x4q_textbook_proof_20260524.json,
// the same anchor the L0 Tc xval qforge_qe_xval_test.hexa consumes). LaH10 and
// Li2MgH16 are EXPLICIT "pending" placeholders — their QE-DFPT λ·Tc have NOT yet
// landed (their gate pods 38943553·38922322 are still computing; READ-ONLY, never
// touched here). Their numeric fields are 0.0 sentinels and are NEVER compared;
// they keep the aggregate HELD until the real λ·Tc are folded in. No fabrication.
//
// ── PROVENANCE (CaH6 reference λ — RE-ANCHORED 2026-06-02, d6 honesty) ────────
// The gate REFERENCE is a literature/QE TARGET (the value QFORGE-NC must reproduce
// to flip the migration default); it is NOT a QFORGE measurement. This brick only
// corrects that TARGET — the QFORGE-measured λ (mga_cah6_qforge_lambda, lane A/B's
// live work) is untouched.
//
//   ANCHOR (active) — Sci. Rep. 14 (2024) s41598-024-69190-0 (PMC11310335),
//     "fully ab initio Eliashberg" CaH6 Im-3m @ 170 GPa:
//       λ = 2.27 · 96×96×96 k · 8×8×8 q · self-consistent G · screened μee=0.137
//       (harmonic DFPT; paper Tc = 236 K via full screened-Coulomb Eliashberg).
//     PRESSURE-MATCHED to the campaign's own QE run (170 GPa) → we pair this λ
//     with the campaign-measured ω_log = 1236.4 K @170 GPa (apples-to-apples P).
//     μ* = 0.13 here (the campaign's CaH6 Tc-vs-measurement comparison μ*).
//     Re-derived reference Tc:
//       • allen_dynes_full(2.27, 1236.4, 1236.4, 0.13) = 206.8 K  (f1-only, ω̄₂=ω_log;
//         🟢 hexa verify --expr allen_dynes_full 2.27 1236.4 1236.4 0.13 206.811 --tol 0.01)
//       • allen_dynes_full(…, 0.10)                    = 223.0 K
//       • mcmillan_tc(1236.4, 2.27, 0.13)              = 181.3 K  ← the Tc_QE_K field
//         below (the gate test's internal mcmillan-consistency value, kept green).
//     The f1-only allen_dynes Tc UNDER-estimates the paper's full-Eliashberg 236 K
//     (expected: no screened-Coulomb f2 lift) — recorded honestly, not tuned.
//   ALTERNATE — Wang, Tse, Tanaka, Iitaka, Ma, PNAS 109, 6463 (2012)
//     (arXiv:1203.0263, the canonical CaH6 discovery paper) @ 150 GPa: λ = 2.69,
//     Eliashberg Tc = 220–235 K (μ*=0.10/0.13). allen_dynes_full(2.69, 1236.4,
//     1236.4, 0.13) = 235.6 K lands AT the top of Wang's published band. Not the
//     active anchor only because its pressure (150 GPa) ≠ the campaign ω_log P
//     (170 GPa); Sci.Rep.2024 is pressure-matched + denser-mesh-documented.
//
// ── SUPERSEDED PRIOR VALUE (preserved for audit, d_defer_no_delete + d6) ──────
//   λ = 4.376 · ω_log = 1236.4 K · μ* = 0.10 · Tc(McMillan) = 255.1 K, from
//   rtsc_cah6_dft_4x4x4q_textbook_proof_20260524.json. TRACEABLE but NOT a
//   converged published value: it is the broad_Ry=0.015 row — the SOFTEST/lowest
//   el_ph_sigma of that QE run's 10-broadening sweep, where λ over-counts. The SAME
//   record's λ-ladder falls 4.376→3.403 as broadening tightens (0.015→0.030) and its
//   own literature_harmonic field reads "1.5–3.0"; the record's preferred Tc-vs-
//   measured match uses the broad=0.030 row (λ=3.403, Tc 213 K vs measured 215 K),
//   NOT the 4.376 row. Every converged published CaH6 (Im-3m) λ @150–250 GPa sits
//   at 1.6–2.7 (Wang 2012: 2.69 · Sci.Rep.2024: 2.27/1.92/1.62). So 4.376 is an
//   under-converged near-soft-mode artifact, ~1.6–2.7× the converged value.
//   Retained verbatim in mga_cah6_superseded_4376() below for the audit trail.
//
// A "record" is a flat [status, λ_QE, ω_log_K, μ_star, Tc_QE_K]. status:
//   1.0 = terminal (real QE {λ,Tc}; compared)   0.0 = pending (placeholder; HELD)

// CaH6 — TERMINAL (RE-ANCHORED to the converged published λ; see PROVENANCE).
// [status, λ_QE, ω_log_K, μ*, Tc_QE_K] — Tc_QE_K = mcmillan_tc(ω_log, λ, μ*) so the
// gate test's internal Tc-consistency check stays green; the SCIENTIFIC re-anchored
// reference Tc is the allen_dynes_full value 206.8 K (μ*=0.13), recorded above.
pub fn mga_cah6() -> [float] {
    return [1.0, 2.27, 1236.4, 0.13, 181.256]
}

// CaH6 — SUPERSEDED prior reference (un-converged broad=0.015 / near-soft-mode
// value λ=4.376, ω_log=1236.4, μ*=0.10, Tc=255.1). PRESERVED for audit per
// d_defer_no_delete + d6 — superseded by Sci.Rep.2024 λ=2.27 (see PROVENANCE).
// NOT consumed by the gate (kept as a frozen audit record only).
pub fn mga_cah6_superseded_4376() -> [float] {
    return [1.0, 4.376, 1236.4, 0.10, 255.1]
}

